      "locked": false,
      "text": "Templates for this round: \n\n\n\n1. Understand the requirements. ( template )\n\n -> read the requirements or problem statement.\n -> ask doubt , under the overall flow, different flows.\n -> just understand it.\n -> don't think about the entities , method etc. \n -> just understand like normal DSA problem something \n    interview also tell method.\n -> once clear about requirements or problem. \n -> jump to coding.\n\n\n\n2.  How to code this problem ( template )\n\n\n -> write one class to solve the problem \n    and its multiple method will solve multiple problem. \n\n\n -> as per requirements create the attributes.\n    -> attribute here can be simple data type like int, string etc. \n    -> or it can be data structure like vector, list, queue etc.\n    -> or it can be class or class in vector , list , queue etc. \n\n    -> if you think partcular part require to have another class \n        create that\n\n        -> for example: \n            -> we need to store user's name \n            -> rather than writing list of string for user name.\n            -> create anther class name as \"user\" \n            -> write name in \"user\" class\n            -> then create list of user , instead string. \n\n            -> here we might need to implement operation overloading as well in \n                case if we are using sorting etc. or map\n            -> make sure to have constructor default or normal. \n            -> and we can use interface or abstract class here\n            -> like let say splitwise expense -> it can have differen type so in that case. \n\n   -> after this create the constructor -> for initialising these things. \n        -> in c++ make sure to create default constructor else can break.\n\n   -> we usually don't require but when require , we might need to create\n        -> destructor\n        -> default constructor -> do this always. \n        -> or might need copy constructor as well. \n\n   -> once we have attribute, write one method to solve the problem use these\n      attribute. \n   -> this method is similar to your dsa problem, ist just this you are inside method\n      and have to deal with classes. \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Templates for this round: \n\n\n\n1. Understand the requirements. ( template )\n\n -> read the requirements or problem statement.\n -> ask doubt , under the overall flow, different flows.\n -> just understand it.\n -> don't think about the entities , method etc. \n -> just understand like normal DSA problem something \n    interview also tell method.\n -> once clear about requirements or problem. \n -> jump to coding.\n\n\n\n2.  How to code this problem ( template )\n\n\n -> write one class to solve the problem \n    and its multiple method will solve multiple problem. \n\n\n -> as per requirements create the attributes.\n    -> attribute here can be simple data type like int, string etc. \n    -> or it can be data structure like vector, list, queue etc.\n    -> or it can be class or class in vector , list , queue etc. \n\n    -> if you think partcular part require to have another class \n        create that\n\n        -> for example: \n            -> we need to store user's name \n            -> rather than writing list of string for user name.\n            -> create anther class name as \"user\" \n            -> write name in \"user\" class\n            -> then create list of user , instead string. \n\n            -> here we might need to implement operation overloading as well in \n                case if we are using sorting etc. or map\n            -> make sure to have constructor default or normal. \n            -> and we can use interface or abstract class here\n            -> like let say splitwise expense -> it can have differen type so in that case. \n\n   -> after this create the constructor -> for initialising these things. \n        -> in c++ make sure to create default constructor else can break.\n\n   -> we usually don't require but when require , we might need to create\n        -> destructor\n        -> default constructor -> do this always. \n        -> or might need copy constructor as well. \n\n   -> once we have attribute, write one method to solve the problem use these\n      attribute. \n   -> this method is similar to your dsa problem, ist just this you are inside method\n      and have to deal with classes. \n",
